# Example ReRDMFT input file: LiH, 6-31G, GNOF, FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE with FIXED_OCCUPANCIES
# TRUE -- the occupation-number optimization still runs once at the starting HF orbitals (see
# "Optimized geminal occupation numbers" below), but the macro loop itself never re-optimizes
# them again: each macro-iteration only re-optimizes the orbitals at those fixed occupations
# (watch for "occupations-fixed" on every line of the iteration table). This is therefore a pure
# orbital optimization at fixed occupation numbers, and converges to a HIGHER (worse) energy than
# lih_gnof_full_optimization.inp's usual alternation of orbital and occupation optimization --
# expected, since fixing one of the two coupled variables can only ever match or lose against
# optimizing both.
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 2
PNOF_COUPLING 2
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
FIXED_OCCUPANCIES TRUE
USE_RI FALSE  # preserve this example's pre-existing dense/Cholesky path (USE_RI now defaults TRUE)

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.594900
END
